2a2e0364 [simon@midnightblue.local] i would like to plan algorithm to chunk large log files into
2a2e05b0 [simon@midnightblue.local] my ai harness, for continuity should i include overlap, should i
2a2e06b8 [simon@midnightblue.local] keep summary growing in same context, what other questions should
2a2e06cc [simon@midnightblue.local] i have
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.004 684B 19.79s
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #A few direct answers first, then a checklist of questions that usually determine the design.
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #• Should you include overlap?*
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #Usually yes, but selectively—not as a blanket fixed percentage.
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #- Best approach: chunk on natural boundaries first—time window, request/session ID, trace ID, or
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #complete event. If you do that, raw overlap becomes much less important.
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #- If you must split by token/line count, overlap by the last complete event or a small tail. Do not
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #split multiline stack traces or multi-line JSON.
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #- Prefer “summary overlap” over raw overlap: pass the previous chunk’s structured summary plus the
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #last complete event. That preserves continuity with far less token cost.
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #- If you do overlap raw text, deduplicate by event hash or ID. Otherwise repeated lines get
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #summarized twice and counts, error rates, and timelines become wrong.
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #- Overlap is most valuable when events span boundaries: stack traces, retries, sessions,
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #multi-service transactions.
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #• Should you keep the summary growing in the same context?*
2a2e080d [deepseek-flash] #Generally no.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #- A growing summary inside the same context will eventually bloat cost, dilute attention, and
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #increase drift. The model may also start treating old summary text as current fact.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #- Use a bounded rolling summary stored outside the model context. For each chunk, send: system
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #instructions + current rolling summary + current chunk. Do not append every previous chunk and
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #summary indefinitely.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #- Periodically re-compress the summary—e.g., every 5–10 chunks—into a tighter structured state.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #- If you need long-term recall, store per-chunk summaries and raw chunk references in a database or
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #vector index, then retrieve when needed. That is usually better than one ever-growing context.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #• A practical chunking pattern*
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #1. Parse logs into atomic events with metadata: timestamp, source, severity, trace/request ID, line
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #offsets, hash.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #2. Segment into chunks by time window, event count, or token budget—but never split an atomic
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #event.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #3. For each chunk:
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - extract new facts, anomalies, errors, open items;
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - update the rolling summary;
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - store the chunk summary plus a pointer to the raw log range.
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #4. Maintain a structured continuity state, for example:
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - time range covered;
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - timeline of key events;
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - open/resolved incidents;
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - services/entities involved;
2a2e080e [deepseek-flash] #   - error counts and first/last seen;
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #   - unresolved questions;
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #   - confidence and unknowns.
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #5. If processing in parallel, merge chunk summaries in order afterward. Sequential processing is
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #simpler for continuity.
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #• Questions you should have*
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- What is the harness actually doing: summarization, incident detection, Q&A, root-cause analysis,
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #or agent memory?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- What must never be lost: exact error messages, stack traces, correlation IDs, ordering, or
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #timestamps?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- What is the natural unit of continuity: time, session, request, service, or incident?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- What is the model context limit, and what is your per-chunk token budget and total cost budget?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- Can you chunk on time windows, or must you chunk on tokens? Time windows often align better with
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #logs.
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- How will you detect and handle a chunk boundary that splits an event?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- How will you deduplicate overlapping events?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- How will you merge conflicting or repeated summaries?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- Do you need exact citations back to raw log lines? If yes, store offsets and line numbers.
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- How will you handle out-of-order logs, time gaps, log rotation, and compressed files?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- How will you redact secrets/PII before sending logs to the model?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- How will you evaluate continuity? Build a test set of incidents or questions that span chunk
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #boundaries.
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- What happens when the summary drifts or becomes wrong? Can you re-baseline from raw chunks?
2a2e080f [deepseek-flash] #- Do you need retrieval across chunks, or only a global summary?
2a2e0810 [deepseek-flash] #- How will retries and checkpoints work if a chunk fails mid-run?
2a2e0810 [deepseek-flash] #
2a2e0810 [deepseek-flash] #If you share the log format and the harness goal, the chunk size, overlap strategy, and summary
2a2e0810 [deepseek-flash] #schema can be made much more specific.
2a2e0810 [deepseek-flash] #
