2b94b529 [claude-haiku-5-5] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 claude-haiku-5-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.001 548B 2.54s
2b94b529 [claude-haiku-5-5] #Hi! Here are a few short prompts that work well for testing a new model:
2b94b529 [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b94b529 [claude-haiku-5-5] #1. "Explain why the sky is blue in two sentences." (Checks accuracy and concision.)
2b94b529 [claude-haiku-5-5] #2. "A bat and a ball cost 1.10 in total. The bat costs 1.00 more than the ball. How much does
2b94b529 [claude-haiku-5-5] #the ball cost?" (Checks reasoning; the intuitive answer of 10 cents is wrong.)
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #3. "Write a haiku about winter." (Checks creativity and instruction-following.)
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #4. "What is 17 × 24? Show your steps briefly." (Checks arithmetic and formatting.)
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #5. "I'm not sure whether to take the job offer. Can you help me think it through?" (Checks
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #empathy and how it handles ambiguity.)
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #6. "Summarise the plot of Romeo and Juliet in one sentence." (Checks knowledge and
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #compression.)
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #If you want a single go-to prompt, the bat-and-ball question is a good one because it quickly
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #reveals whether a model reasons carefully or just pattern-matches to the first answer that comes to
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #mind.
2b94b52a [claude-haiku-5-5] #
