2b95b402 [claude-haiku-5-5] #Thanks for testing this. An empty `thinking` string in the block doesn't necessarily mean something
2b95b402 [claude-haiku-5-5] #is broken, but a few things commonly cause it:
2b95b402 [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b95b402 [claude-haiku-5-5] #1. Streaming accumulation. When streaming, the `content_block_start` event for a thinking
2b95b402 [claude-haiku-5-5] #block usually carries `thinking: ""`. The actual text arrives afterward in `content_block_delta`
2b95b402 [claude-haiku-5-5] #events with `thinking_delta` payloads. If the harness reads the field from the start event and
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #never appends the deltas, it will see an empty string even though the content streamed correctly.
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #2. Thinking not enabled for the request. If the extended thinking parameter wasn't sent, or
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #the budget was set too low, the model may return little or no thinking text.
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #3. Redacted thinking. Some blocks come back as `redacted_thinking` with an encrypted `data`
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #field instead of readable text. A harness expecting `thinking` text may treat these as empty.
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #4. Signature-only blocks. A thinking block can include a `signature` with an empty or
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #minimal `thinking` field, particularly in multi-turn flows where earlier blocks are passed back.
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #To narrow it down, check the raw event stream or non-streamed JSON for the block type, whether
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #`thinking` is empty in the raw payload or only in your parsed output, and whether a `signature` is
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #present. If the raw payload is empty too, the issue is likely on the request side. If only your
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #parsed output is empty, the issue is probably in the accumulation logic.
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #I don't have direct access to my own reasoning content, so I can't confirm what the block should
2b95b403 [claude-haiku-5-5] #contain from my side. If you share the raw block (with anything sensitive removed) or your request
