2b95b403 [roha] anthopic content: [{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This seems like a technical harness question rather than something needing deep reasoning on my end. An empty thinking field is likely just how the system behaves when I don't produce visible reasoning content, not necessarily a bug—I should explain this plainly and suggest they check their API parameters for extended thinking settings.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Thanks for testing this. An empty `thinking` string in the block doesn't necessarily mean something is broken, but a few things commonly cause it:\n\n1. **Streaming accumulation.** When streaming, the `content_block_start` event for a thinking block usually carries `thinking: \"\"`. The actual text arrives afterward in `content_block_delta` events with `thinking_delta` payloads. If the harness reads the field from the start event and never appends the deltas, it will see an empty string even though the content streamed correctly.\n\n2. **Thinking not enabled for the request.** If the extended thinking parameter wasn't sent, or the budget was set too low, the model may return little or no thinking text.\n\n3. **Redacted thinking.** Some blocks come back as `redacted_thinking` with an encrypted `data` field instead of readable text. A harness expecting `thinking` text may treat these as empty.\n\n4. **Signature-only blocks.** A thinking block can include a `signature` with an empty or minimal `thinking` field, particularly in multi-turn flows where earlier blocks are passed back.\n\nTo narrow it down, check the raw event stream or non-streamed JSON for the block type, whether `thinking` is empty in the raw payload or only in your parsed output, and whether a `signature` is present. If the raw payload is empty too, the issue is likely on the request side. If only your parsed output is empty, the issue is probably in the accumulation logic.\n\nI don't have direct access to my own reasoning content, so I can't confirm what the block should contain from my side. If you share the raw block (with anything sensitive removed) or your request parameters, I can help you work out which case you're hitting."}]
