2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #specifically for complex reasoning. With these models, the reasoning process is enabled by default.
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #You can also control whether the thought process is returned in the API response using the
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #`thinkingConfig` parameter inside your generation configuration.
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #When enabled, the model returns its reasoning as a separate part of the response payload, marked
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #with a `thought` boolean property, alongside the final answer.
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #2. Chain-of-Thought Prompting (Standard Models)
2b966871 [gemini-4-argon] #If you are using standard models (like `gemini-1.5-pro` or `gemini-1.5-flash`), there is no API
