2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 gemini-4-argon 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.004 9.411KB 7.86s
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #Here are the specific terms for the leftover sediment, solids, and waste in winemaking, brewing,
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #and distilling:
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• In Winemaking*
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• Lees: The primary term for the sediment that settles at the bottom of the fermentation
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #vessel, consisting primarily of dead yeast cells and tiny grape particles.
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• Pomace (or Marc): The solid remains of the grapes (skins, pulp, seeds, and stems)
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #left over right after pressing the juice.
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• Must: The freshly pressed grape juice that still contains all the skins, seeds, and stems
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #before fermentation separates them out.
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• In Distilling*
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• Stillage (or Slop / Spent Wash): The acidic liquid and solid residue left
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #behind in the bottom of the still after the alcohol has been boiled off.
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• Dunder: The specific term used in rum production for the yeast-rich, liquid residue left
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #in the still after distilling cane juice or molasses.
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• Pot Ale: Used in malt whisky distilling for the copper-rich residue left at the bottom of
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #the first distillation (the wash still).
2c3ea7f3 [gemini-4-argon] #• Foreshots, Heads, and Tails (or Feints): The impure liquid fractions that
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #come off the still at the very beginning and very end of a run, which are separated from the
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #drinkable "heart."
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #• In Brewing (Beer & Mash)*
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #• Trub: The layer of heavy sediment (fats, proteins, hop residue, and inactive yeast) left
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #at the bottom of the fermenter or kettle.
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #• Draff (or Spent Grain): The exhausted grain solids left over after mashing
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #(extracting the sugars with hot water).
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #• General / Literary Terms*
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #• Dregs: The most common everyday term for the last, unwanted bits of sediment at the
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #bottom of a barrel, bottle, or glass.
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #• Barm: The thick, foamy yeast scum that rises to the top of fermenting liquor or
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #beer.
2c3ea7f4 [gemini-4-argon] #
